cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GPCR Sonification — β2-Adrenergic Receptor: an open-source pipeline
  for the sonification and cross-modal validation of GPCR molecular
  dynamics
message: >-
  If you use this software or its outputs, please cite the Zenodo
  deposit listed below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ekrem"
    family-names: "Yasar"
    email: "eyasar@erzincan.edu.tr"
    affiliation: "Department of Biophysics, Erzincan Binali Yildirim University, Erzincan, Turkey"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0575-7267"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER
    description: Zenodo archive of the released source code and assets
repository-code: "https://github.com/eygpcr/gpcr-sonification-beta2ar"
url: "https://github.com/eygpcr/gpcr-sonification-beta2ar"
abstract: >-
  An open-source pipeline that maps activation-related geometric
  features extracted from β2-adrenergic receptor (β2AR) molecular
  dynamics trajectories onto musical parameters, renders the result as
  MIDI / WAV audio through three timbres, builds synchronised protein-
  cartoon videos and an interactive HTML player, and computationally
  validates information preservation by Random Forest cross-modal
  classification, leave-one-instrument-out generalisation, and
  canonical correlation analysis between the MD and audio feature
  spaces. Applied as a proof of concept to three GPCRMD β2AR
  trajectories (inactive, active apo, active + orthosteric agonist),
  the pipeline transfers to other GPCRs and allosteric MD systems
  without code changes beyond residue selection.
keywords:
  - sonification
  - molecular dynamics
  - GPCR
  - β2-adrenergic receptor
  - cross-modal classification
  - canonical correlation analysis
  - auditory display
  - open science
  - reproducible research
